1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,860
Two thousand three hundred seventy-eight
dollars.

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:07,710
That's what one extra dollar of income
costs a retired couple in Medicare
premiums

3
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:09,040
for twenty twenty-seven.

4
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:11,100
Not one dollar of tax.

5
00:00:11,820 --> 00:00:13,280
One dollar of income…

6
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:16,880
that crosses a line Medicare published
this week.

7
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:18,980
This is Run the Number.

8
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:23,610
Medicare released the official twenty
twenty-seven Part B numbers on November

9
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:24,800
seventeenth.

10
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:29,430
By the end you'll know what the new
premium takes out of your January raise,
where

11
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:33,700
the six income lines sit, and which year's
tax return decides your premium.

12
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:36,180
This is education, not advice.

13
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,980
The couple is an example, not a real
person.

14
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:40,780
The premium first.

15
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:45,320
The standard Part B premium for twenty
twenty-seven is two hundred nine dollars

16
00:00:45,370 --> 00:00:46,740
and forty cents a month.

17
00:00:47,260 --> 00:00:50,060
That's six dollars and fifty cents more
than this year.

18
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:52,920
The Part B deductible goes to two hundred
ninety-two dollars,

19
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:54,920
up nine.

20
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:59,260
The hospital deductible, Part A, goes to
one thousand seven hundred seventy-six.

21
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:01,680
Now the raise.

22
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:06,280
Social Security's cost of living
adjustment for January is three point six
percent.

23
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,940
On the average retirement check, Social
Security says that's about seventy-five

24
00:01:10,990 --> 00:01:12,080
dollars a month.

25
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:15,460
Part B comes out of that check before it
reaches you.

26
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:18,000
So the six fifty is taken off the top.

27
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:20,610
Seventy-five in, six fifty out.

28
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:24,530
The premium takes about one dollar of
every eleven in the raise.

29
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:29,610
On a fifteen hundred dollar check the
raise is fifty-four, and the premium takes

30
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:30,660
one in eight.

31
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:32,600
Smaller check, bigger bite.

32
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:34,280
That part is ordinary.

33
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:35,960
It happens every January.

34
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:39,500
The part that isn't ordinary is the
surcharge.

35
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:45,480
Medicare charges higher earners more for
the same Part B.

36
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:51,200
The I R S calls it I R M A A, the
income-related monthly adjustment amount.

37
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:52,760
Call it the surcharge.

38
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:57,300
It has six steps, and twenty
twenty-seven's lines were published this
week.

39
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:01,640
For a couple filing jointly, the first
line is two hundred twenty-four thousand

40
00:02:01,690 --> 00:02:02,690
dollars.

41
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:06,440
Under it, each spouse pays the standard
two hundred nine forty.

42
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,740
One dollar over it, each spouse pays two
hundred ninety-three ten.

43
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:14,760
That's eighty-three seventy more, each,
every month.

44
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:18,340
Add the Part D surcharge, fifteen forty
each.

45
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:20,420
Two people, twelve months.

46
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:24,110
Two thousand three hundred seventy-eight
dollars and forty cents…

47
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:25,740
for the year.

48
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:27,380
For one dollar.

49
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:29,160
The lines keep going.

50
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:31,410
Two hundred eighty-two thousand.

51
00:02:31,460 --> 00:02:32,710
Three hundred fifty-four.

52
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:34,000
Four hundred twenty-four.

53
00:02:34,050 --> 00:02:35,340
Seven hundred fifty.

54
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:40,710
At the top, each spouse pays seven hundred
eleven dollars and eighty cents a month

55
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:42,020
for Part B alone.

56
00:02:42,420 --> 00:02:46,350
Twelve thousand dollars a year more than
the couple under the first line, for

57
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:47,400
the same card.

58
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:50,580
For a single filer, cut every line in
half.

59
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:53,520
The first one is one hundred twelve
thousand.

60
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:56,500
Here's the part that catches people.

61
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:59,940
Medicare doesn't look at what you earn in
twenty twenty-seven.

62
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:03,140
It looks at your tax return from two years
back.

63
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:07,720
Your twenty twenty-seven premium is set by
your twenty twenty-five return.

64
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:13,170
The income on that return is modified
adjusted gross income: your adjusted gross

65
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:15,580
income, plus tax-exempt interest.

66
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:18,180
Line eleven, plus line two a.

67
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:20,040
Now the couple.

68
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:23,100
Both sixty-eight, on Medicare, filing
jointly.

69
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:27,720
In twenty twenty-five their income was two
hundred fourteen thousand dollars:

70
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:30,540
pensions, Social Security, some dividends.

71
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:32,640
Ten thousand under the line.

72
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:37,010
In December that year they converted
twenty thousand dollars from a traditional

73
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:38,620
I R A to a Roth.

74
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:43,630
Sensible on its face: twenty thousand at
twenty-two percent is forty-four hundred

75
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:47,140
in tax, paid now so it grows tax-free
later.

76
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:48,860
Run the number.

77
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:53,000
Two hundred fourteen plus twenty is two
hundred thirty-four thousand.

78
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:55,240
Over the first line by ten thousand.

79
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:58,320
In twenty twenty-seven, the surcharge
arrives:

80
00:03:58,960 --> 00:03:59,980
two thousand three hundred seventy-eight

81
00:04:00,030 --> 00:04:01,700
dollars for the year.

82
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:04,190
The conversion didn't cost forty-four
hundred.

83
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:07,400
It cost sixty-seven hundred seventy-eight.

84
00:04:07,450 --> 00:04:09,800
Thirty-four percent, not twenty-two.

85
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:14,940
Had they converted ten thousand instead of
twenty, they'd have landed at two hundred

86
00:04:14,990 --> 00:04:16,280
twenty-four thousand exactly.

87
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Under the line.

88
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:20,700
Twenty-two hundred in tax, no surcharge.

89
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:24,230
The second ten thousand is the one that
cost twenty-three hundred seventy-eight

90
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:26,600
dollars on top of its own tax.

91
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,440
Now the fine print.

92
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:29,880
Three lines.

93
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:30,830
One.

94
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:32,960
The surcharge resets every year.

95
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:36,180
One high year costs you one year, two
years later.

96
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:37,720
It isn't permanent.

97
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:42,840
But a Roth conversion, a house sale, a big
capital gain, a pension lump sum…

98
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:44,620
each one is a year.

99
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,010
Two.

100
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:47,060
The lines move.

101
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:51,900
Twenty twenty-six's first line for a
couple was two hundred eighteen thousand.

102
00:04:51,950 --> 00:04:54,360
Twenty twenty-seven's is two hundred
twenty-four.

103
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:58,550
They're indexed to inflation, but the line
that will judge your twenty twenty-six

104
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:00,500
income hasn't been published yet.

105
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:02,060
Leave room.

106
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,070
Three.

107
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:04,120
There's an appeal.

108
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:08,640
If your income dropped because of a life
change, retirement, a spouse's death,

109
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:13,800
divorce, losing a pension, you can ask
Social Security to use a more recent year.

110
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:16,100
Form S S A dash forty-four.

111
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:17,820
It's two pages.

112
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:21,100
People pay the surcharge for years without
filing it.

113
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:22,660
How to check yours.

114
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:24,780
Pull your twenty twenty-five return.

115
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:27,230
Line eleven plus line two a.

116
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:30,560
Hold it against two hundred twenty-four
thousand for a couple,

117
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:32,420
one hundred twelve for a single.

118
00:05:32,860 --> 00:05:35,880
That's your twenty twenty-seven premium,
already decided.

119
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:37,320
Then look at this year.

120
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:42,490
Whatever you do with the I R A before
December thirty-first lands on the twenty

121
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:43,540
twenty-eight bill.

122
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:44,820
Here's the pattern.

123
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,200
Six fifty a month is the number in the
headline.

124
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:50,200
It's real, and it takes a bite out of the
raise.

125
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:52,490
But the lines are where the money is.

126
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:56,520
A couple who knows where the first line
sits can keep a conversion a thousand

127
00:05:56,570 --> 00:05:57,640
dollars under it.

128
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,880
A couple who doesn't pays twenty-three
hundred dollars for the dollar that
crossed.

129
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:07,310
A fee-only fiduciary or a C P A, with the
return in front of them, can run the

130
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:10,280
exact number before the conversion, not
after.

131
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:12,800
One thing this week.

132
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:15,460
Find line eleven on last year's return.

133
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:18,240
Write the twenty twenty-seven line next to
it.

134
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:23,000
Then decide what this December's I R A
moves do to the twenty twenty-eight
number.

135
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:25,360
New numbers every Tuesday and Friday.

136
00:06:25,980 --> 00:06:27,840
Subscribe so the next one finds you.

137
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:30,140
Will your money last as long as you do?

